'''Ariranha''' (from the [[Kurupiran languages|Aruanãyará]] ''arerãîa''; {{Literal translation|water jaguar|otter}}) was an indigenous leader who led his people in resistance against territorial incursion by settlers backed by the [[Anyos Federales|Baliscan government]] of [[Josèp Bernat]] during the [[Cantonal War]]. He represented the [[Yaruanãyará tribe]] at the [[1883 Confederal Convention]]. 

